marta: Quick presales ask from Apollo Health. They need a one-paragraph copy/paste runbook for SDK streaming (hosted), ephemeral handshake, tiny node snippet for tool/function calls and structured JSON output validation. Can someone paste a minimal version? :pray:
ben: Hosted POC — keep it simple. Steps: 1) presales ephemeral token, 2) init SDK with credentialProvider, 3) open WebSocket w/ subprotocol `rwd-stream-v1`, 4) send `meta` with `schema_id`, 5) handle `toolcall` -> reply `tool_response`.
li: Streaming knobs I recommend: max_inflight=6, heartbeat=20s, client-side inflight queue + exponential backoff on 429. For bursty work use short batch REST calls.
marta: Can you drop a one-paragraph runbook + curl + tiny Node example I can paste?
ben: One-paragraph runbook (copy/paste): "POST to `https://presales.redwood.ai/v1/ephemeral` with your account id to get an ephemeral token. Use that token in the Redwood SDK `credentialProvider` to open a streaming connection to `wss://stream.redwood.ai/v1?model=<model>` with subprotocol `rwd-stream-v1`, send a `meta` JSON frame including `schema_id` (set `strict:true` to enable server-side schema validation), stream inputs, and respond to `toolcall` frames with corresponding `tool_response` frames. For sustained high throughput ask for a short Dedicated trial or use batch REST endpoints. Example handshake curl: `curl -X POST https://presales.redwood.ai/v1/ephemeral -H 'Authorization: Bearer PRESALES_KEY' -d '{"account":"apollo-health"}'`." 
li: Tiny Node snippet to paste:
```js
const client = new RedwoodClient({ credentialProvider: async () => ({ token: await getEphemeral() }), streaming: true });
const stream = await client.stream({ model: 'rwd-4-small', multiplex: true });
stream.send({ type: 'meta', schema_id: 'apollo-v1', strict: true });
stream.on('message', async (m) => {
  if (m.type === 'toolcall') {
    const res = await callExternal(m.args);
    stream.send({ type: 'tool_response', id: m.id, result: res });
  }
});
```
ben: Cost hint for presales: 40 req/s @ ~1k tokens is large if run 24/7 (billions/day). For a business-hours POC or short demo run it's usually a few thousand USD; recommend a 1-hour representative run to measure real token usage and then we can give a firmer ballpark.
ops-bot: presales/apollo-runbook v1 deployed to presales-bucket (files: runbook.md, node-example.js) :white_check_mark:
marta: Perfect — I'll send this to the customer and schedule a 30m demo. Ping here if they ask for SOC2/KMS details so we can loop security. :thumbsup:
